menu "JK BMS Monitor Configuration"

    config JK_WIFI_SSID
        string "WiFi SSID"
        default "SET_ME"
        help
            Network the board should join.

    config JK_WIFI_PASS
        string "WiFi password"
        default "SET_ME"

    config JK_MQTT_URI
        string "MQTT broker URI"
        default "mqtt://SET_ME:1883"
        help
            Broker address, e.g. mqtt://192.168.1.50:1883. This is the Home
            Assistant broker, not HA's web UI port.

    config JK_MQTT_USER
        string "MQTT username"
        default ""
        help
            Leave empty for an anonymous broker; the client then connects with
            no credentials rather than with an empty username.

    config JK_MQTT_PASS
        string "MQTT password"
        default ""
        help
            Deliberately empty. Anything set here is compiled into the binary
            and written to sdkconfig, which is a file you will eventually
            share or commit.

    config JK_CELL_COUNT
        int "Number of cells in the pack"
        range 1 32
        default 16
        help
            Used only to decide how many per-cell Home Assistant entities to
            announce. Discovery is published when MQTT connects, which is
            before the first frame arrives, so the count cannot be read from
            the BMS in time. The published cell values themselves come from
            the frame's own presence bitmap, not from this.

    config JK_BAUD
        int "RS485 baud rate"
        default 115200
        help
            115200 for the 55AA push stream on RS485-P.

    config JK_EXPIRE_S
        int "Home Assistant expire_after (seconds, 0 = disabled)"
        default 30
        help
            Marks entities unavailable if no state message arrives within this
            many seconds. This is the only thing that catches a wedged
            publisher: the availability topics cover a clean disconnect and an
            LWT, but a task that hangs mid-loop leaves the last retained values
            looking live forever.

            Must comfortably exceed the real data cadence or entities will
            flap. Measured on this unit: one DYNAMIC frame per ~6.4 s scan
            cycle. 30 s covers four missed cycles.

endmenu
